{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73002"] :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/worked-solution "The given expression is a product of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $2!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n2!=2\\cdot 1=2.\n$$\n\n- Computing $3!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n3!=3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2!\\,3! & =2!\\cdot 3! \\\\ & =2\\cdot 6 \\\\ & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
